title: 'Gnomon onboarding MVP-a: Provisioner engine + guided `gnomon setup`'
summary: 'Founder ruling (2026-10-19): launching gnomon or the app on a fresh Mac must guide setup in a real UI; the CLI verbs stay. Arky''s design (a setup-mode loopback endpoint, one engine, two renderers) was reconciled with Aegis''s threat model: the digest is shown only on the user''s own launch surface (the terminal or the wrapper window), and nothing in a browser can start provisioning. MVP-a extracted identity init into an event-emitting Provisioner (identity-cli output byte-identical), added read-only preflight, a guided `gnomon setup`, bare-gnomon routing, and completeDevice for the identity.json-written-but-no-registry-row crash window. Invariants I1–I10 have falsifiers. MVP-b (GUI screens, wrapper Phase::Setup, presence.available helper op) is in progress.'
